{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Full handfuls.</b> This amount would not have sufficed for all of Egypt. Therefore one must say that the boils came on their own, not from the soot, except that the Holy One, blessed be He, does not wish to change the way of the world, and does something like the customary practice in part." "<b>Full handfuls of soot.</b> Live coals — ריקול״ט in Old French — from the root נופח, blowing on coals of fire." "<b>And Moses threw it heavenward.</b> In many places the air is called שמים. And from the air it scattered and fell upon all of them."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:56:40.987966126Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}